module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentGrothendieck
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RepresentedQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleAffineSectionBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleExtensionQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleKernelQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentSiteEquivalenceOfUniv
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Abelian.SerreClass.WeakInverseImage

/-!
# Quasi-coherent modules on the small étale site of a scheme, at a free module universe

Let `T` be a scheme in a big étale site `E`.  Descent, Lemma 0GNB lists closure properties of the
quasi-coherent modules on the small étale site `T_ét`; this library proves them in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallEtaleQuasicoherentAbelian`,
`…SmallEtaleQuasicoherentExtensions` and `…SmallEtaleQuasicoherentWeakSerre` for module sections
in the universe `u` of the schemes, by transport along Stacks 03DX (2), whose Zariski side is
Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`, a single-universe category.  That universe is too
small for the stacks chapters: a direct image of modules on an algebraic stack has its sections
in `Type (u + 1)`, so the quasi-coherence conditions there are read at module universe `u + 1`,
and a module at that universe is not in general a universe lift of one at `u` (a quasi-coherent
module is locally a cokernel of a map of direct sums indexed by types in `Type (u + 1)`).

This file proves the closure properties at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`, for every `m`:
kernels, cokernels, extensions, colimits of every shape in that universe, and a zero object.

## The route

No Zariski module category at a larger universe is needed.  The small étale site of an algebraic
space is treated by this library at the module universe `max (u + 1) m` directly
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isClosedUnderKernels`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isClosedUnderCokernels`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isClosedUnderExtensions` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape`, proved from the cartesian criterion on
affine étale charts).  A scheme `T` lying in a big fppf site `B` is the algebraic space
`yoneda.obj U` of an object `U` of `(Sch/T)_fppf`, and the small étale site of that space is
equivalent, as a ringed site, to the small étale site of `T` in the big étale site
`AlgebraicGeometry.associatedBigEtaleSite B`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representedSmallEtaleEquivalence`, the two structure sheaves matching by
`rfl`).  Quasi-coherence is invariant under an equivalence of ringed sites at any module universe
containing the site (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.SiteTransport.isQuasicoherentOnSite_transport_iff`),
and an equivalence of module categories is exact, so each closure property pulls back.

Finally the big étale site `E` is arbitrary, subject to having the cutoff of `B`: the category
`T_ét` and its structure sheaf only see the cutoff, and its topology, generated by the étale
coverings bounded by the site's covering cardinal, is the étale precoverage of all schemes pulled
back along the inclusions (`AlgebraicGeometry.smallEtale_precoverage_eq_comap` and the two
identifications above it), so it does not depend on the other data of `E` either.  This is the
situation of the stacks chapters, whose big étale and big fppf sites are tied by `E.cutoff =
B.cutoff`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isClosedUnderKernels_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isClosedUnderCokernels_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse`
  and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isClosedUnderExtensions_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse`:
  **Descent, Lemma 0GNB (3) and the three cases of (4)** at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`.
* `SmallEtale.isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse`:
  **Descent, Lemma 0GNB (2)** at that universe, for every shape in it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.containsZero_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse`: a zero
  module is quasi-coherent.

## Implementation notes

The statements are theorems, not instances: they need a big fppf site with the cutoff of `E`,
which instance search cannot supply, and abelian structures on module categories at a raised
universe are deliberately not global instances in this library (see the notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/QuasicoherentWeakSerreUnconditional.lean`).

No `stacks` attribute is carried: Descent, Lemma 0GNB is registered at the universe of the
schemes, and these are the same clauses at a larger universe of module sections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GNB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GNB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03M1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DM)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe m u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

/-- The closure properties of quasi-coherence at the module universe `max (u + 1) m` that this file
transports, bundled so that one transport argument serves all of them. -/
abbrev QuasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C]
    {J : GrothendieckTopology C} (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}) : Prop :=
  (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m} R).IsClosedUnderKernels ∧
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m} R).IsClosedUnderCokernels ∧
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      R).IsClosedUnderExtensions ∧
    ∀ (K : Type (max (u + 1) m)) [Category.{max (u + 1) m} K],
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
        R).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape K

/-- The closure properties only depend on the underlying presheaf of rings and on the topology,
which may be given by two propositionally equal terms. -/
theorem quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_of_eq {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C]
    {J₁ J₂ : GrothendieckTopology C} (hJ : J₁ = J₂) (R₁ : Sheaf J₁ RingCat.{u})
    (R₂ : Sheaf J₂ RingCat.{u}) (hR : R₁.obj = R₂.obj)
    (h : QuasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse.{m} R₂) :
    QuasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse.{m} R₁ := by
  subst hJ
  obtain rfl : R₁ = R₂ := by
    cases R₁
    cases R₂
    cases hR
    rfl
  exact h

/-- **The closure properties on the small étale site of a represented scheme.**  For an object `U`
of the big fppf site over `S`, the small étale site of its underlying scheme, in the big étale
site carried by the same category of schemes, is equivalent as a ringed site to the small étale
site of the algebraic space `yoneda.obj U`; quasi-coherence corresponds across the equivalence of
module categories, which is exact, and the closure properties hold on the side of the algebraic
space at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`. -/
theorem quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_represented (B : BigFppfSite.{u})
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) (U : BigFppfOver B S hS) :
    QuasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse.{m}
      (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B S hS U) := by
  let : HasSheafify (Space.representedSchemeSmallEtaleTopology B S hS U)
      AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m, u, u + 1} _
  let : (Space.representedSchemeSmallEtaleTopology B S hS U).WEqualsLocallyBijective
      AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m,
      u + 1, u} _
  let : HasSheafify (Space.SmallEtale.topology B S hS (yoneda.obj U))
      AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m, u, u + 1} _
  let : (Space.SmallEtale.topology B S hS (yoneda.obj U)).WEqualsLocallyBijective
      AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m,
      u + 1, u} _
  let : Abelian (SheafOfModules.{max (u + 1) m}
      (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B S hS U)) :=
    SheafOfModules.instAbelian.{max (u + 1) m, u, u, u + 1} _
  let : Abelian (SheafOfModules.{max (u + 1) m}
      (Space.representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS U)) :=
    SheafOfModules.instAbelian.{max (u + 1) m, u, u, u + 1} _
  let e := Space.representedSmallEtaleEquivalence B S hS U
  let Φ : SheafOfModules.{max (u + 1) m} (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B S hS U) ≌
      SheafOfModules.{max (u + 1) m} (Space.representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS U) :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.reindexEquivalence e (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B S hS U)
  let P' := SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
    (Space.representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS U)
  have hP : SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B S hS U) = P'.inverseImage Φ.functor :=
    funext fun M => propext
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.SiteTransport.isQuasicoherentOnSite_transport_iff.{u + 1, u, u, u, m}
        e (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B S hS U) M).symm
  have hF := AlgebraicGeometry.isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS U
  have : P'.IsClosedUnderKernels := Space.isClosedUnderKernels.{m} B S hS (yoneda.obj U) hF
  have : P'.IsClosedUnderCokernels := Space.isClosedUnderCokernels.{m} B S hS (yoneda.obj U) hF
  have : P'.IsClosedUnderExtensions :=
    Space.isClosedUnderExtensions.{m} B S hS (yoneda.obj U) hF
  have hcol : ∀ (K : Type (max (u + 1) m)) [Category.{max (u + 1) m} K],
      P'.IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape K := fun K _ =>
    Space.isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape.{m} B S hS (yoneda.obj U) hF K
  rw [QuasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse, hP]
  refine ⟨ObjectProperty.isClosedUnderKernels_inverseImage P' Φ.functor,
    ObjectProperty.isClosedUnderCokernels_inverseImage P' Φ.functor, inferInstance,
    fun K _ => ?_⟩
  have := hcol K
  infer_instance

/-- The topology on the small étale site of a scheme is the étale precoverage of all schemes pulled
back along the inclusions. -/
private theorem topology_eq_comap_etalePrecoverage (E : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (T : Scheme.{u})
    (hT : E.Contains T) :
    topology E T hT = (((Scheme.etalePrecoverage.comap E.inclusion).comap
      (Over.forget (E.obj T hT))).comap (inclusion E T hT)).toGrothendieck := by
  rw [topology, smallEtale_precoverage_eq_comap E ⟨T, hT⟩, bigEtaleOver_precoverage_eq_comap E T hT,
    bigEtalePrecoverage_eq_comap E]

/-- **The closure properties on the small étale site of a scheme, for an arbitrary big étale site
with the cutoff of a big fppf site.**  The scheme is represented over itself in the big fppf
site, and the small étale site in `E` is the small étale site in
`AlgebraicGeometry.associatedBigEtaleSite B`: the two categories and structure sheaves agree once
the cutoffs are identified, and the two topologies are both the étale precoverage of all schemes
pulled back along the inclusions. -/
theorem quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_structureSheaf (B : BigFppfSite.{u})
    (E : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (h : E.cutoff = B.cutoff) (T : Scheme.{u}) (hT : E.Contains T) :
    QuasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse.{m} (structureSheaf E T hT) := by
  have hT' : B.Contains T := lt_of_lt_of_eq hT h
  have key := quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_represented.{m} B T hT'
    (Over.mk (𝟙 (B.obj hT')))
  have hE := topology_eq_comap_etalePrecoverage E T hT
  have hE' := topology_eq_comap_etalePrecoverage (associatedBigEtaleSite B) T hT'
  cases E
  dsimp only at h
  subst h
  exact quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_of_eq (hE.trans hE'.symm) (structureSheaf _ T hT)
    (Space.representedSchemeStructureSheaf B T hT' (Over.mk (𝟙 (B.obj hT')))) rfl key

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (E : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (h : E.cutoff = B.cutoff) (T : Scheme.{u})
  (hT : E.Contains T)

include h

/-- **Descent, Lemma 0GNB (3), kernel clause, at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`**: a kernel
of a morphism of quasi-coherent modules on the small étale site of a scheme is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isClosedUnderKernels_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      (structureSheaf E T hT)).IsClosedUnderKernels :=
  (quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_structureSheaf.{m} B E h T hT).1

/-- **Descent, Lemma 0GNB (3), cokernel clause, at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`**: a
cokernel of a morphism of quasi-coherent modules on the small étale site of a scheme is
quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isClosedUnderCokernels_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      (structureSheaf E T hT)).IsClosedUnderCokernels :=
  (quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_structureSheaf.{m} B E h T hT).2.1

/-- **Descent, Lemma 0GNB (4), the extension case, at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`**: the
middle term of a short exact sequence of modules on the small étale site of a scheme whose outer
terms are quasi-coherent is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isClosedUnderExtensions_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      (structureSheaf E T hT)).IsClosedUnderExtensions :=
  (quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_structureSheaf.{m} B E h T hT).2.2.1

/-- **Descent, Lemma 0GNB (2), at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`**: a colimit, of any shape
in that universe, of quasi-coherent modules on the small étale site of a scheme is
quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isClosedUnderColimitsOfShape_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse
    (K : Type (max (u + 1) m)) [Category.{max (u + 1) m} K] :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      (structureSheaf E T hT)).IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape K :=
  (quasicoherentClosuresFreeModuleUniverse_structureSheaf.{m} B E h T hT).2.2.2 K

omit h in
/-- A zero module on the small étale site of a scheme, at the module universe `max (u + 1) m`, is
quasi-coherent, so quasi-coherence contains a zero object there. -/
theorem containsZero_isQuasicoherentOnSite_freeModuleUniverse :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, max (u + 1) m}
      (structureSheaf E T hT)).ContainsZero := by
  let : HasSheafify (topology E T hT) AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m, u, u + 1} _
  let : (topology E T hT).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m,
      u + 1, u} _
  let : Abelian (SheafOfModules.{max (u + 1) m} (structureSheaf E T hT)) :=
    SheafOfModules.instAbelian.{max (u + 1) m, u, u, u + 1} _
  exact SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_containsZero

end AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

end
